From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leaf Performance experiments <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Sep 2026 02:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid map tracking predicate allocations

Problem reference: Paper issue #9597 (accepted performance issue).
Implementation: independently adapted to current Leaf 26.2 applied sources.
License: GPL-3.0-only as part of the distributed Leaf server patch stack.

MapItemSavedData repeatedly scans player inventories while tracking map
holders. Use a specialized inventory scan so each scan no longer allocates a
capturing Predicate. This intentionally does not add cross-call caching or
change per-stack decoration, frame, renderer, or packet semantics.
diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Inventory.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/player/Inventory.java
